  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "qjqLzfCaAQ0OvAoe699gYjHzTew=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:08.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "# document model structure has metadata specifications and modules\n\nA document model consists of three layers:\n\n1. **Basic Metadata** \u2014 `id`, `name`, `extension`, `description`, `author` (name + website)\n2. **Specifications** \u2014 Versioned specs containing `version`, `changeLog`, and `state` definitions (global/local with schema, initialValue, examples)\n3. **Modules** \u2014 Operational modules that group related operations\n\nThe metadata identifies the model. The specifications define its state shape. The modules organize what operations can be performed on that state.\n\nSince [[document models have 37 available operations across 7 categories]], the operations for building a document model span header setup, module creation, operation definition, and state schema configuration.\n\n---\n\nTopics:\n- [[schema design]]",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T12:35:08.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:08.000Z"
    }
  },
